    "# Challenges and Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "Applying machine learning to electromagnetic design is non-trivial. While the potential benefits are enormous, several significant challenges must be addressed. This chapter explores the key limitations and the solutions developed in this work to overcome them."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Data Generation Cost\n",
    "\n",
    "### Problem: Deep Learning Requires Thousands of Labeled Examples\n",
    "\n",
    "The fundamental challenge of supervised learning is the massive data requirement:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Computational Cost:**\n",
    "- **Each training sample** = 1 FEA simulation = 1-2 hours\n",
    "- **Typical CNN training** = 10,000 samples = 10,000-20,000 hours\n",
    "- **Total data generation time** = **1-2 years of computation**\n",
    "- **Hardware requirements** = Multiple workstations running continuously\n",
    "\n",
    "**Financial Cost:**\n",
    "- **Cloud computing costs** = $10,000+ for training datasets\n",
    "- **Software licenses** = $5,000+ for commercial FEA packages\n",
    "- **Personnel costs** = Engineering time for simulation setup and monitoring\n",
    "- **Total investment** = $20,000+ per trained model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Data Generation Cost Analysis\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simulation parameters\n",
    "fea_time_hours = 2  # hours per simulation\n",
    "fea_cost_per_hour = 5  # $/hour for computing resources\n",
    "engineer_cost_per_hour = 75  # $/hour for personnel\n",
    "overhead_factor = 1.5  # overhead multiplier\n",
    "\n",
    "# Data requirements for different models\n",
    "models = {\n",
    "    'Simple CNN': {'samples': 5000, 'training_time': '12 hours'},\n",
    "    'Complex CNN': {'samples': 10000, 'training_time': '15 hours'},\n",
    "    'RNN (Performance Maps)': {'samples': 15000, 'training_time': '3 hours'},\n",
    "    'Ensemble Model': {'samples': 20000, 'training_time': '20 hours'},\n",
    "    'Transfer Learning': {'samples': 3000, 'training_time': '8 hours'}\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Data Generation Cost Analysis ===\")\n",
    "print(\"Model                | Samples | FEA Time | Computing Cost | Engineer Cost | Total Cost\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 85)\n",
    "\n",
    "total_costs = []\n",
    "sample_counts = []\n",
    "model_names = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for model_name, params in models.items():\n",
    "    samples = params['samples']\n",
    "    fea_time = samples * fea_time_hours\n",
    "    computing_cost = fea_time * fea_cost_per_hour\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Assume 10% engineer overhead for setup and monitoring\n",
    "    engineer_time = fea_time * 0.1\n",
    "    engineer_cost = engineer_time * engineer_cost_per_hour\n",
    "    \n",
    "    total_cost = (computing_cost + engineer_cost) * overhead_factor\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"{model_name:<20} | {samples:>7} | {fea_time:>8.0f}h | ${computing_cost:>12.0f} | ${engineer_cost:>12.0f} | ${total_cost:>9.0f}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    total_costs.append(total_cost)\n",
    "    sample_counts.append(samples)\n",
    "    model_names.append(model_name)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualize cost analysis\n",
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cost vs samples\n",
    "colors = plt.cm.viridis(np.linspace(0, 1, len(model_names)))\n",
    "bars1 = ax1.bar(model_names, total_costs, color=colors, alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Model Type')\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('Total Cost ($)')\n",
    "ax1.set_title('Data Generation Cost by Model Type')\n",
    "ax1.set_xticklabels(model_names, rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
    "ax1.grid(True, alpha=0.3, axis='y')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add value labels on bars\n",
    "for bar, cost in zip(bars1, total_costs):\n",
    "    height = bar.get_height()\n",
    "    ax1.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2., height + max(total_costs)*0.01,\n",
    "             f'${cost:,.0f}', ha='center', va='bottom', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cost per sample\n",
    "cost_per_sample = [cost/samples for cost, samples in zip(total_costs, sample_counts)]\n",
    "bars2 = ax2.bar(model_names, cost_per_sample, color=colors, alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel('Model Type')\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('Cost per Sample ($)')\n",
    "ax2.set_title('Cost Efficiency Analysis')\n",
    "ax2.set_xticklabels(model_names, rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
    "ax2.grid(True, alpha=0.3, axis='y')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add value labels on bars\n",
    "for bar, cost in zip(bars2, cost_per_sample):\n",
    "    height = bar.get_height()\n",
    "    ax2.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2., height + max(cost_per_sample)*0.01,\n",
    "             f'${cost:.2f}', ha='center', va='bottom', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Time analysis\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Time Investment Analysis ===\")\n",
    "print(\"Assuming parallel computation on 10 workstations:\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "for model_name, params in models.items():\n",
    "    samples = params['samples']\n",
    "    total_hours = samples * fea_time_hours\n",
    "    parallel_hours = total_hours / 10\n",
    "    parallel_days = parallel_hours / 24\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"{model_name}:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Sequential time: {total_hours/24:.1f} days ({total_hours/168:.1f} weeks)\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Parallel time (10 workstations): {parallel_days:.1f} days\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Training time: {params['training_time']}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Total project time: {parallel_days + 0.5:.1f} days\")\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Key Insights:\")\n",
    "print(\"• Transfer learning reduces data requirements by 70-85%\")\n",
    "print(\"• Parallel computation is essential for practical data generation\")\n",
    "print(\"• Computing costs are significant but manageable for research/industrial applications\")\n",
    "print(\"• Engineer time is a major component of total cost\")"
   ]
  },
  {
